nd getting things done in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Causatives <span class=\"italic\">Get </span>and<span class=\"italic\"> Have</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use a causative verb when we want to talk about something that someone else did for us. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"strong\">get / have</span> when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Get </span> usually means \"to convince to do something\" or \"to trick someone into doing something\".", "type": "text"}, {"content": "[get + person + to + verb]", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>My boss <span class=\"strong\">got her to work</span> late on Tuesday. </li> <li> Did the boss <span class=\"strong\">get you to work</span> on Saturday?</li></ul> </span>(My boss convinced these people to do something.) <br> <br> [get + object + past participle] <br> For example:<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li> I had to <span class=\"strong\">get the work done</span> on time.</li></ul>  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have </span></br>{have + object + verb} or {have + object + past participle} ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have</span>  means to give someone the responsibility to do something.<br/><br/> For example:<br> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Dr. Smith <span class=\"strong\">had his nurse take</span> the patient's temperature. <li>Please<span class=\"strong\"> have your secretary fax </span>me the information.</span><li><span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">had the windows washed</span>.</span></li></ul> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes, you use<span class=\"italic\"> get</span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have</span> is a little more neutral.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My professor got me to take some courses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We got our workers to use inPrint for layout here too. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " My supervisor had me apply many of these skills. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There was a crisis and my boss had me help. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "What-Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are used to help us focus on a particular part of the sentence and to emphasise what we want to say by introducing it as a relative clause.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are usually linked to the clause that we want to focus on with <span class=\"strong\">is</span> or <span class=\"strong\">was</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare:    <ul>       <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span> I am looking for is a new secretary.    </br>       A new secretary is <span class=\"strong\">what I</span> am looking for.</ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are often used with verbs like <span class=\"strong\">adore</span>, <span class=\"strong\">dislike</span>, <span class=\"strong\">enjoy</span>, <span class=\"strong\">hate</span>, <span class=\"strong\">like</span>, <span class=\"strong\">hope</span>, <span class=\"strong\">love</span>, <span class=\"strong\">need</span>, <span class=\"strong\">prefer</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">want</span>.<ul><span class=\"strong\">What</span> I<span class=\"strong\"> hate</span> most about going to a job interview is the waiting.      </br>   <span class=\"strong\">   What</span> I<span class=\"strong\"> liked</span> most about their company was the people.</span></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What-clauses are also often used with <span class=\"strong\">does/do/did </span>and when we want to give emphasis to the whole sentence, rather than a particular clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare:       <ul>   <span class=\"italic\"> The manager interviewed all the salespeople first.  </br><span class=\"strong\">         What </span>the manager <span class=\"strong\">did</span> first <span class=\"strong\">was</span> interview all           the salespeople.</span></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These sentences are useful in writing where we cannot use intonation for emphasis, but they are also often used in speech.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now what we are looking for is an editorial assistant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I have your letter of reference from your former editor and what she has to say is very complementary. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What I hoped to achieve by doing that was to ensure that I developed the skills I needed while gaining a plethora of knowledge.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "get down to brass tacks", "type": "name"}, {"content": "get to the point quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Alright, let's get down to brass tacks. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you are talking about your capabilities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "established a good rapport", "type": "name"}, {"content": "worked together on friendly terms", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My boss and I quickly established a good rapport. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "working relationship", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way two people work together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I had a good working relationship with my boss.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hands-on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "practical; not theoretical", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My professor got me to take some courses that were more hands-on.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meet deadlines", "type": "name"}, {"content": "complete work at the expected time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Occasionally, there was a crisis and I had to meet deadlines.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm proper interview etiquette.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a poster displaying my ideas in a creative concept.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain why I think certain \"dos\" and \"don'ts\" are very important.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, brainstorm all the things people should do in an interview and all the things people shouldn't do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Establish which are the most important.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a poster for the wall with pictures of job interview \"dos\" and job interview \"don'ts.\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Get your pictures from the Internet or magazines and make a collage.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Display the posters around the room.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With your partner, make a short presentation explaining your poster.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}